<title>UK: BICC gets go ahead for Edinburgh hospital.</title>
<headline>BICC gets go ahead for Edinburgh hospital.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>British engineering and construction group BICC Plc said on Tuesday a consortium of which it is part has been given government approval to complete negotiations for a 180 million stg new Royal Infirmary and University Medical School in Edinburgh.</p>
<p>Consort Healthcare, made up of BICC, Royal Bank of Scotland Plc and Morrison Construction Group Plc, hopes to complete the negotiations before the end of 1997.</p>
<p>Royal Bank of Scotland will provide the finance in conjunction with a group of leading banks. Design and construction will be undertaken by BICC subsidiaries, who will work with Morrison Construction.</p>
</text>
